# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
# NOTE: these are PYTHON BUILD artifacts and must be anchored to the repo root. As a bare `lib/` the
# rule matched at ANY depth, so every NEW file added to a loop's editable_files/lib/ was silently
# ignored -- species_priors.py (the copy that makes the spacetime loop independent of biological) and
# fair_baseline.py (which defines what every fair-gain on the board MEANS) were both untracked and would
# have been lost. Files already moved in with `git mv` stayed tracked, which is why it went unnoticed.
/lib/
/lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# Virtual Environment
venv/
env/
ENV/
.venv/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

